<title>NORWAY: Nycomed 9-month pre-tax falls 32 pct.</title>
<headline>Nycomed 9-month pre-tax falls 32 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30.</p>
<p>				 (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Operating revenue	     5,794	vs	6,211</p>
<p>Operating result		1,037	vs	1,488</p>
<p>Result before tax		 898	vs	1,321</p>
<p>Result after tax		  595	vs	  857</p>
<p>Earnings per share	   5.84 crowns vs    8.67 crowns</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norwegian pharmaceuticals company is Nycomed ASA. The company was listed on the Oslo bourse on May 14 after demerger with energy group Hafslund ASA.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of seven analysts forecast operating profits for the first nine months of 1.05 billion crowns and a result before tax of 913 million crowns. Five of the analysts recommended a hold on the share while two said sell.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
